Bahrain, Kuwait, Puerto Rico, Saudi Arabia, and The Netherlands. Its restaurants provides classic wings, boneless wings, tenders, and hand-sauced-and-tossed in various flavors, as well as chicken sandwiches, fries, and hand-cut carrots and celery that are cooked-to-order. The company was founded in 1994 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael J. Skipworth CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 345 people. Revenue per employee of $2.0M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $306K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $72K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Wingstop Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.3B market cap on $697M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +25% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 55% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 46-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $106M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.88\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.4\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 90% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9015676185108129},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 18% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Could Wingstop (NASDAQ:WING) Digital Strategy Shape Growth?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/how-could-wingstop-nasdaqwing-digital-strategy-shape-growth","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794587160.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.452,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Did Wingstop (NASDAQ:WING) Jump as It Trimmed Its Sales View?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/why-did-wingstop-nasdaqwing-jump-as-it-trimmed-its-sales-view","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794481500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Did Wingstop (NASDAQ:WING) Rally Despite a Trim?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/why-did-wingstop-nasdaqwing-rally-despite-a-trim","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794462000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Wingstop (NASDAQ:WING) Opening Too Fast?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/midcap/is-wingstop-nasdaqwing-opening-too-fast","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794404160.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CenterBook Partners LP Buys New Stake in Wingstop Inc. $WING","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/centerbook-partners-lp-buys-new-stake-in-wingstop-inc-wing.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794215719.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.902,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Jim Cramer shares surprise Wingstop stock target despite fewer customers","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/jim