d little stock (0.7%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 5.9% a year to shareholders (5.2% in buybacks and 0.8% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 14.8% of the float, 2.9 days to cover."],"people":["With about 345 employees, each generates about $2.0M of revenue, 5.3x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 24.5% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $306K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.7M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (10/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $72K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":57,"head":"Avoid: priced 90% above its fair value of $83.54.","pros":["Composite 55, above the 39 line (gates 14/25)","ROIC 55.2% vs WACC 8.9%","FCF margin 15.2%","Revenue grew 22.9%/yr over 5y","26 analysts' mean target $186 (+17%)"],"cons":["Trades 90% above fair value of $83.54","Net debt/EBITDA 5.0x","P/E 37.2x vs sector 18.8x","EV/EBITDA 23.4x vs sector 10.7x","P/FCF 40.7x vs sector 16.7x"],"flags":["Priced 90% above its fair value of $83.54"],"need":[],"buy_below":71.01,"vc":{"base":83.54,"base_src":"dcf","bear":50.99,"bull":132.83,"alt_median":33.02,"n_alt":2,"gap":1.5301,"dispersion":0.2645,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 153% above the other models' median ($33.02)"]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"mc_quantiles":[30.31,43.51,50.99,56.28,60.5,65.45,68.96,72.52,76.6,80.2,84.66,88.56,93.12,97.38,101.32,107.25,114.15,120.18,132.83,148.45,183.77],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.692,"discount_rate":0.247,"terminal_growth":0.016,"exit_multiple":0.046},"ticker":"WING","date":"2026-11-13"}